TITLE:: NdefRackMapper
summary:: the rack's controls as Mapper's targets, and the window's learn through Mapper
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRack, Classes/NdefRackKtl, Classes/NdefRackGUI, Classes/NdefRackModule

DESCRIPTION::
With Mapper (sc-mapper) installed, the rack is one of its providers. While the
rack watches its Ndefs - link::Classes/NdefRack#*watch::, which opening the
window does - it is registered with code::Mapper.default:: under
code::\ndef::, and every control a controller can turn is the target
code::[\ndef, module, control]::.

code::
MKtl(\m1, "akai-midimix");
Mapper.default.map(\m1, \kn_1_1, [\ndef, \lp, \freq]);   // a knob on lp's freq
Mapper.default.learn([\ndef, \lp, \res]);                // the next element moved
NdefRackMapper.gui(\lp, \freq);                          // Mapper's window, lp freq on show
::

table::
## strong::control:: || strong::Mapper's kind:: || strong::what a move does::
## a bar, a stepped bar || code::\knob:: || code::module.set(control, value)::, in the control's spec
## a switch || code::\toggle:: || sets 0 or 1
## a gate || code::\toggle:: || 1 while on, the default back when off - the window's gate button
## a trigger || code::\trigger:: || 1, and the node map clean again 50 ms later
::

Signal inputs and arrays are not targets. A move goes through the module's
link::Classes/NdefRackModule#-set::, so a control with voices sets every voice;
a patched control belongs to its cable and is left alone. The addresses are
names, so a mapping to a module that is not there waits, and works again when
the module is back. Mapper saves the mappings in its own file, not in patch
files.

It is also what the window asks about controllers: learn mode, the control
waiting for an element, what turns a control. With Mapper that is Mapper's -
learn mode is shared with every window Mapper maps -, without it
link::Classes/NdefRackKtl::'s. NdefRackKtl's bindings and follow work either
way.

Mapper is looked up by name; nothing here needs it to compile. Asking for
code::Mapper.default:: the first time reads Mapper's file: a check sets
code::Mapper.defaultPath:: and code::Mapper.autoLoad = false:: before the rack
watches.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: key
The provider key, the first item of every address. Default code::\ndef::.
Change it before the rack first watches, if at all: saved mappings name it.

METHOD:: usesMapper
RETURNS:: true when Mapper is installed - the window's learn is then Mapper's.

METHOD:: mapper
RETURNS:: code::Mapper.default::, or nil without Mapper.

METHOD:: canLearn
RETURNS:: true when the Modality toolkit is installed: the window's learn button is there.

METHOD:: register
Register the rack with code::Mapper.default::. link::Classes/NdefRack#*watch:: does it; again is harmless.

METHOD:: unregister
Take the rack out of Mapper: its mappings wait until it registers again.

METHOD:: isRegistered
RETURNS:: true while the rack is Mapper's provider under link::#*key::.

METHOD:: address
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name
RETURNS:: code::[\ndef, module, param]::

METHOD:: learning
Learn mode: a click on a control in the window arms it. Mapper's
code::learnMode:: with Mapper, else code::NdefRackKtl.learning::. Turned on
here, it is turned off again when the window closes; turned on elsewhere, it
stays.

METHOD:: armed
RETURNS:: code::[module, control]:: waiting for an element, or nil.

METHOD:: learn
The next element moved on any controller turns this control.
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name

METHOD:: cancelLearn
Nothing waits for an element any more.

METHOD:: forget
Nothing turns this control any more: its Mapper mapping and its NdefRackKtl binding go.
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name

METHOD:: controlOf
What turns a control: Mapper's mapping first, then NdefRackKtl's binding or follow.
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name
RETURNS:: an Event code::(ktl:, element:, follow:):: - with code::mapper: true:: for a Mapper mapping - or nil.

METHOD:: gui
Mapper's window - the window's mapper button.
ARGUMENT:: module
optional: with code::param::, the mapping of that control is put on show
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name
RETURNS:: the MapperWindow, or nil without Mapper.

METHOD:: windowClosed
The window calls it when it closes: learn mode off if the rack turned it on.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: mapLabel
RETURNS:: "ndef rack", what Mapper's window calls the rack.

METHOD:: mapTargetAt
ARGUMENT:: path
code::[module, control]::
RETURNS:: the description of one control as Mapper reads it, or nil.

METHOD:: mapTargets
RETURNS:: the descriptions of every control a controller can turn, module by module.

METHOD:: update
NdefRack's notifications: Mapper is told when the targets changed, and when values moved.
ARGUMENT:: who
ARGUMENT:: what
